        {
          "text": "WAN Shou-ch'i 萬壽祺 (T. 年少, 介若, 內景, H. 明志道人, monastic name 慧壽), 1603–1652, June 8, poet, painter, and man of letters, was a native of T'ung-shan, Kiangsu. His great-grandfather came from Nanchang, Kiangsi, and settled in T'ung-shan, the prefectural city of Hsü-chou, for medical practice.",
